<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/000U">Construction <span data-tag="000U">1.2.4.1</span> <span class="named">(The Horn $\Lambda ^{n}_{i}$)</span>.</a> Suppose we are given a pair of integers $0 \leq i \leq n$ with $n &gt; 0$. We define a simplicial set $\Lambda ^{n}_{i}: \operatorname{{\bf \Delta }}^{\operatorname{op}} \rightarrow \operatorname{Set}$ by the formula </p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  ( \Lambda ^{n}_{i} )([m]) = \{  \alpha \in \operatorname{Hom}_{\operatorname{{\bf \Delta }}}([m], [n]): [n] \nsubseteq \alpha ([m] ) \cup \{  i \}  \} . \]
</div>
<p> We regard $\Lambda ^{n}_{i}$ as a simplicial subset of the boundary $\operatorname{\partial \Delta }^{n} \subseteq \Delta ^ n$. We will refer to $\Lambda ^{n}_{i}$ as the <em>$i$th horn in $\Delta ^{n}$</em>. We will say that $\Lambda ^{n}_{i}$ is an <em>inner horn</em> if $0 &lt; i &lt; n$, and an <em>outer horn</em> if $i = 0$ or $i = n$. </p>
</article>
